Ladybird draws a synthesized font with Skia’s embolden and skew, and
synthetic bold leaves glyph advances unchanged. Blink does the same: Its
FontPlatformData sets SkFont::setEmbolden() and a skew of -1/4, and adds
nothing to advances. WebKit’s Font::widthForGlyph() doesn’t add its
synthetic bold offset to advances either, though Gecko’s FreeType
backend does, in GetFTGlyphExtents().
